    "speaker": "client",
    "text": "Marissa,\n\nDevelopment work in preparation for launch has kept me occupied for the past few days, hence the gap in communication. I would now like to resume the website work, as it will clearly be integral to the launch. The areas requiring review and planning are:\n\n1\\. Finalize the assets and layout for the initial landing-page design, including its responsive behavior.\n\n2\\. Establish the basis for later website pages: whether they share common headers and footers, use \"dark mode,\" or have a complementary \"light mode\" style. I mean separate styling, not something users can switch.\n\n3\\. Define guidance and/or rules for responsive behavior in general.\n\n4\\. Work through the layout and styling of the dashboard shell and \"canvas.\"\n\nFor context, I have attached screens from the secure signup and login flow, which uses AWS Cognito. They currently have AWS default styling, although several self-styling options are available.\n\nWhile some of this belongs within the current job, other parts sit outside its scope. What approach would you recommend from here? Would a meeting or video call be the best way to discuss it?\n\nDerek"
  },
